questions_for_the_author [
  "What baseline do the savings refer to: a continued session, a session that auto-compacts, or fresh sessions with a memory file? And on which model and context window?",
  "At what chat length were they measured? Here UniiChat is dearer below roughly 50-90 tool-heavy turns and only then pulls ahead.",
  "What do the compactions cost you, as a share of total spend, at Haiku xhigh? We measured about 11,500 thinking tokens and 46 s per 512-byte line at xhigh.",
  "What is the denominator of 98.6% and 96.2%: all input tokens, or only the tools-system-view prefix? Do they come from the cache model alone, or were they checked against real usage?",
  "Which cache-read and cache-write prices does the design assume, and does 'don't buy 1-hour entries' still hold for a chat a person types into with pauses over 5 minutes?",
  "Are compactions really sent the full tool list, shell included? If so, how often do they call a tool, and what stops a read-only shell command from running?",
  "How often does a turn answer as if it were a compaction (a summary line in place of doing the task)? We saw 12 of 112 turns on Sonnet with the verbatim prompt.",
  "What happens after a turn that adds more than about 84 lines (a 40-tool-call turn)? We measured a full view rewrite on the next call.",
  "Is there evidence that standing orders still govern behaviour once they are gone from every view line, and over how many messages?",
  "Why xhigh? Did lower efforts fail a downstream test, or only miss the 512-byte limit more often on the first try?",
  "How long do users wait in the tail, not on the median, with 8 compactions in flight after a large tool-heavy turn?",
  "Was the design run through a harness that adds its own text around the message (Claude Code, pi under a subscription login), or only on the raw API with a key?"
]
