compactor_tradeoff "E4, one corpus of 128 messages, one run per candidate. All compaction figures below recomputed from the rows and match.\n\n| | Haiku low | Haiku high | Haiku xhigh |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Cost per built line, CLI USD | 0.00135 | 0.00246 | 0.00657 |\n| Wall per built line | 6.5 s | 15.5 s | 47.7 s |\n| First try within 512 bytes | 94/171 (55%) | 144/178 (81%) | 174/179 (97%) |\n| Sends per line | 1.86 | 1.19 | 1.03 |\n| Thinking tokens per send | 462 | 2,954 | 11,572 |\n| Sends that called a tool | 4 of 318 | 0 of 212 | 0 of 184 |\n| Standing rules at level 5 (n=13) | 9 | 12 | 12 |\n| Corrected values at level 3 / level 5 (n=10) | 6 / 7 | 10 / 10 | 10 / 8 |\n| Sonnet reader, 40 questions | 38 | 40 | 38 |\n| Haiku reader, two runs | 32, 31 | 35, 35 | 29, 31 |\n\nWhat low effort gives up against xhigh:\n- **Size fit on the first try:** almost half the lines need a resend, and one line was kept at 519 bytes.\n- **Discipline about tools:** 4 wasted sends in E4. In E5, where the compactor could see the shell tools, 11.2% of sends (266 of 2,383) ended as a tool call and had to be redone; this stalled the run once, at turn 37.\n- **Standing rules and corrections deep in the tree:** 3 fewer rules at level 5 and 4 fewer corrected values at level 3.\n- **Nothing measurable downstream:** the reader scores are within one run's noise (the Haiku reader's two runs differ by up to 2 of 40 on the same tree).\n\nWhat it gains: 4.9x lower cost and 7.3x less wall time per line; the whole tree in 593 s against 5,558 s.\n\nOther candidates:\n- **Haiku high** is the safer middle: no tool calls, 12 of 13 rules and 10 of 10 corrections at level 5, 40 of 40, at 1.8x low's cost. It was not used in the long replay.\n- **Haiku medium** costs 18% more than low and lost the most rules at level 5 (8 of 13).\n- **Sonnet** is not a cheaper compactor: 0.0150-0.0155 USD per line, about 11x Haiku low, with 0 thinking tokens at both efforts. Tested on 32 messages only (45 lines each) and 10 questions.\n- **A local model:** not tested; none was loaded and loading one was not allowed.\n\nMethod correction that came out of E4: the CLI's cost figure accumulates within a process. Summing it per row overstates retry-heavy arms (0.412 naive against 0.231 corrected for Haiku low; I get the same). Round 1's E1 USD figures for arms with retries are overstated for that reason; nobody recomputed them."
